Nevertheless, as noted in the Green case, a few jurisdictions have refused to depart from a restrictive notion of what constitutes pecuniary loss. The current version of the New York wrongful death statute still talks in terms of “pecuniary injury.” N.Y.Est.Powers & Trusts L. § 5–4.3 (McKinney 1995). Clearly, however, the trend is to permit recovery either by express statutory provision or by judicial interpretations of statutes that widen the scope of recovery. For example, the Texas Supreme Court’s decision in Sanchez v. Schindler, 651 S.W.2d 249 (Tex.1983), interpreted the wrongful death statute’s
